This project focuses on developing an autonomous agent capable of navigating a randomly generated grid environment to collect scattered keys while avoiding wall obstacles. Developed in Python using the PySimpleGUI library for the graphical interface, the agent relies on Reinforcement Learning principles, specifically Policy/Value Iteration. It evaluates the environment by creating a "valueMap" with an integrated reward system and a discount rate (gamma) to continuously calculate the most efficient path. The final application features three difficulty levels (Easy, Medium, and Hard) and includes a functional reset mechanism to overcome edge-case bugs, such as infinite loops or instances where the agent gets trapped.
